{
  // The DOM-libbed home for DOM-COUPLED NON-`.tsx` tests (UNIFIED-VERIFICATION-DESIGN.md §3 — the
  // type-membership floor). The three long-standing type programs partition tests by DIRECTORY + suffix:
  // the DOM-less root graph (`tsconfig.json`) owns node `tests/**`, and the browser packages' tsconfigs
  // reach back into `tests/{client,ui}/**/*.tsx` WITH dom. That leaves a HOLE: a `.ts` (not `.tsx`) test
  // that is DOM-COUPLED — it can't be renamed `.tsx` (the vitest int lane is `.ts`-only, renaming loses
  // execution), and its subject drags a DOM barrel into the node graph (phantom lib.dom errors), so the
  // graph `exclude`s it — and being a `.ts`, no `*.tsx` reach-back claims it either. It would be checked
  // by NO static stage. This config is that missing home: a dom+dom.iterable+es2025 program (the browser
  // lib set, copied from packages/client/tsconfig.json) that OWNS the DOM-coupled `.ts` escapees.
  //
  // WIDENED 2026-09-02 (#1228, the DOM-lib-leak defuse): a `/// <reference lib="dom" />` triple-slash
  // directive is PROGRAM-scoped, not file-scoped — one such line in one root-aggregator-swept file
  // (scripts/probes/st-goldens/generate-goldens.ts) silently supplied lib.dom to the ENTIRE root
  // aggregator, masking every OTHER DOM-coupled escapee riding the same leak. Removing the leak exposed
  // further escapee shapes this program also owns, per-file, same doctrine (never a directory glob
  // beyond the ratified `tests/e2e/**` exception): a DOM-coupled `scripts/**` script (no lib.dom of its
  // own program otherwise), several DOM-coupled `tests/tooling/**` int/CT tests, and ONE DOM-coupled
  // `.ct.tsx` file living outside `tests/{client,ui}/**` (so no package's `.tsx` reach-back claims it
  // either — `jsx: react-jsx` above already anticipated this shape). ONE further escapee this sweep
  // found — tooling/src/snap/ops/appearance-invariant-runtime.ts — turned out NOT to belong here: its
  // only two DOM-typed call sites were converted to Playwright's string-body `.evaluate()` form (same
  // convention the file already used elsewhere), so it needs no dom lib and stays DOM-less in the root
  // aggregator, its natural home (its caller, tooling/src/snap/ops/run.ts, is live production CLI code
  // that could never itself move to a DOM-having program).
  //
  // The `tests-type-membership` verify stage (tooling/src/verify/ops/tests-type-membership.ts) is the permanent
  // guard: it reconciles EVERY type-relevant file under tests/** + playwright/** against the import-closure
  // of every type program (this one included), and REDs if any file lands in zero programs. A new
  // DOM-coupled `.ts` test → add it to the `include` here (the stage names it + this file as the fix).
  //
  // NODE-context: like the root graph, these tests run under vitest/node and may import node:* harness
  // code, so `@types/node` is on (the browser packages' own tsconfigs stay `types: []` — this is a TEST
  // program, not package source, so it does not weaken kit-purity: that is per-package + the dep-cruiser
  // gate, never this config). DOM lib coexists with node here BECAUSE these are browser-subject tests that
  // never touch the server's looser node BodyInit/BlobPart (the 2026-06-28 dom-vs-node incident was SERVER
  // src under dom; test code isn't server src).
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // BUNDLER here, deliberately, while tsconfig.base.json is nodenext (tsx-shedding stage 4). This
    // aggregator EXCLUDES packages/{ui,client}/src as roots but still pulls them in TRANSITIVELY, and
    // those packages' real resolver is vite. Checking them under node-strict resolution makes tsc pick
    // different third-party declaration files than the ones that actually ship (echarts resolved two ways
    // => phantom type-identity mismatches). NODENEXT ENFORCEMENT LIVES WHERE NODE RUNS: each of
    // packages/{server,kit,contracts,db} is checked under nodenext by its OWN tsconfig via the
    // per-package `pnpm typecheck` — that is the stage-4 guarantee, and it is not weakened here.
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",

    // `esnext.disposable` mirrors tsconfig.base.json's lib (node-26 adoption program §1.1) — this array
    // OVERRIDES the base's, so the entry must be repeated here or DOM-coupled tests lose `using` typing.
    "lib": ["es2025", "esnext.disposable", "esnext.temporal", "dom", "dom.iterable"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "types": ["node"],
    // The escapees import their subjects (and sibling harnesses) with explicit `.ts` extensions (tsx-run
    // + the `#imports` map); permit that to typecheck them (safe under the base's `noEmit`).
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true
  },
  // The DOM-coupled `.ts` tests the root graph EXCLUDES and no `*.tsx` reach-back claims — plus (since
  // #1228) the `scripts/**` script, the `tooling/src/**` source file, and the one `.ct.tsx` outside
  // `tests/{client,ui}/**` that rode the dom-lib leak (see the header note above). Per-file escapees are
  // enumerated EXPLICITLY (not a glob) so each is a deliberate add — the membership stage names each one
  // as it appears. Keep in sync with tsconfig.json's matching `exclude` entries (the graph must NOT also
  // own them). EXCEPTION — `tests/e2e/**` rides as a DIRECTORY glob (owner ruling, 2026-07-24): the whole
  // playwright e2e tree is DOM-context by nature (`page.evaluate` callbacks read browser state), not a
  // per-file escapee; DOM-less typing forced hand-rolled element bridges + `as unknown as` casts in every
  // spec.
  "include": [
    "reset.d.ts",
    // The root ambient pair (node-26 adoption program §1.2) — see tsconfig.base.json's include note.
    "platform.d.ts",
    // The ambient side-effect-CSS declaration @orb/ui's own program picks up via `include: ["src"]`. A
    // test here that reaches a client feature front door pulls `@orb/ui/markdown/math.ts` (a bare
    // `import "katex/…​.css"`) into THIS closure, and a d.ts is not part of an import closure — without
    // this line the program REDs on a stylesheet that resolves fine in every real build.
    "packages/ui/src/markdown/css-modules.d.ts",
    "tests/client/features/chat/hooks/use-message-items.test.ts",
    "tests/client/forms/create-form-handle-bridge.test.ts",
    "tests/client/forms/entity-form-base.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/create-entity-draft-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-group-registry.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-section-partition.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-section-registry.test.ts",
    // #1228: the DOM-barrel hazard, chat-feature-barrel flavor — value-imports 2 pure functions from
    // `@orb/client/features/chat`, whose barrel re-exports `chat-list-surface.tsx` (DOM-coupled) →
    // phantom lib.dom errors in the DOM-less node program. The barrel SOURCE stays dom-typechecked by
    // packages/client/tsconfig.
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/join-token.test.ts",
    // #1228: the DOM-lib-leak defuse. Neutralizing scripts/probes/st-goldens/generate-goldens.ts's
    // former `/// <reference lib="dom" />` (a program-scoped triple-slash directive that had been
    // silently supplying lib.dom to the WHOLE root aggregator) reds every one of the escapees below —
    // each is a genuinely DOM-coupled `.ts`/`.ct.tsx` file that was riding the leak instead of being
    // explicitly homed. Each is documented at its own use site; this program is their real home.
    "scripts/probes/st-goldens/generate-goldens.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/accessible-names.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/autosave-status-transcript.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/canvas-ink.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/drop-files.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/held-portrait-image.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/measure-clamp.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/part-vs-surface.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/pixel-contrast.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/scroll-containing-block.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/settings-geometry.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/tier-liveness.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/touch-floor.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/weave-drive.ts",
    "tests/tooling/_shared/browser.int.test.ts",
    "tests/tooling/design-audit-walker.ct.tsx",
    "tests/tooling/snap/cascade.suite.int.test.ts",
    "tests/tooling/snap/ops/contrast.int.test.ts",
    "tests/tooling/stack/lib/engine-launch.test.ts",
    "tests/ui/charts/meter/waystone-treatment.test.ts",
    // #1243, Arm A-prime — the fork ledger for #1228's residual (types:graph 454/45 → 0/0, see
    // packages/client/src/{data,lib,state}/pure.ts): these deep-import a client SOURCE file directly
    // (the pre-existing "Deep import the PURE module, not the barrel" convention — see
    // tests/client/data/import-bundle.test.ts's own comment), and that file is ITSELF DOM-coupled —
    // not reachable through a pure surface at all, so per the fork's own escape clause ("never force
    // it") these tests are homed here instead of minted a pure re-export.
    "tests/client/data/auth-bootstrap.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/auth-config.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/stale-session.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/message-actions-reveal.test.ts",
    // Same fork, SOURCE-internal-`#data` flavor: route-guards.ts itself (not the test) imports the
    // FULL `#data` internal alias (package.json's `"#*": "./src/*/index.ts"` always resolves to the
    // barrel, never the pure subpath) for reasons unrelated to what this test exercises — no pure
    // surface can intercept an internal package-alias import without editing route-guards.ts itself
    // (src churn, out of the fork's fence).
    "tests/client/features/auth/lib/route-guards.test.ts",
    // Same fork, agent-nav flavor: `buildAgentNav` (the ONE export the test needs) is defined in
    // agent-nav/index.ts itself, which imports panel-request.ts (DOM-coupled) at module scope — no
    // separable pure symbol exists.
    "tests/client/agent-nav/index.test.ts",
    // Same fork, forms flavor: `mirrorDraft`/`readDraftSeed` share ONE FILE (entity-form-base.ts) with
    // `focusFirstInvalidField` (`document.querySelector`) — same shape as agent-nav above, no separable
    // pure symbol. `createAutosaveEntityForm` (the fourth) is defined in a `.tsx` React component.
    "tests/client/features/character/lib/character-draft-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/preset/lib/preset-draft-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/world-info/lib/entry-draft-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/forms/create-autosave-entity-form-model.test-d.ts",
    // #1243 final leg (owner-accepted plan change, bridge 178): STOP minting pure surfaces for the
    // tail — the ledger below can shrink later; a red types:graph taxes every lane now. Same shape as
    // agent-nav above: buildAgentNav-style barrels whose ONE export is defined in the barrel file
    // itself, which imports lib/agent-bridge.ts (DOM-coupled) at module scope.
    "tests/client/agent-rpg/index.test.ts",
    "tests/client/agent-seed/index.test.ts",
    // Same final leg, SOURCE-internal-`#data` flavor (route-guards.ts precedent above): each of these
    // deep-imports a client feature lib/ file that itself imports the internal `#data` alias (always
    // index.ts, never the pure subpath) for reasons unrelated to what the test exercises.
    "tests/client/features/workloads/lib/workloads-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/workloads/lib/portability-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/chat-documents-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/persona/lib/persona-editor-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/discovery/lib/corpus-faces.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/chat-books-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/character/lib/character-card-form-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/chat-summary-row.test.ts",
    // The plain `.test.ts` sibling of the already-homed `.test-d.ts` above — same entity-form-base.ts
    // chain (create-autosave-entity-form-model.ts -> use-app-form.ts -> bound-fields/*.tsx).
    "tests/client/forms/create-autosave-entity-form-model.test.ts",
    // #1243, pure.ts #lib-trim displacement: these needed a symbol from a state/data pure.ts member
    // that was removed for internally importing "#lib" (see packages/client/src/{state,data}/pure.ts's
    // own headers for the full member list and rationale) - so they revert to the bare barrel import
    // and move here.
    "tests/client/state/active-chat-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/bus/apply-chat-bus-event.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/chat-stream.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/config/lib/config-search.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-group-registry.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-section-partition.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-section-registry.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-teach.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/create-gated-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/create-gated-store.test-d.ts",
    "tests/client/state/assemble-chrome.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/bus/room-registry.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/invalidation.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/invalidation-carrier.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/invalidation-reads.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/query-client.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/session-freshness.test.ts",
    // #1243: two more #data-internal-alias reachers found on the re-measure after the pure.ts trim -
    // preflight-warn.ts -> use-refinery-schemas.ts -> "#data", and workloads-schedule-model.ts ->
    // workloads-model.ts -> "#data" (workloads-model.test.ts's OWN import was already homed above, but
    // workloads-schedule-model.ts reaches the SAME impure file via a second, independent test).
    "tests/client/features/refinery/lib/preflight-warn.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/workloads/lib/workloads-schedule-model.test.ts",
    // #1243: use-orb-socket.ts imports "../stale-session.ts" directly (not via the "#data" alias this
    // time, a plain relative import) which chains to auth-bootstrap.ts/auth-config.ts - the same
    // DOM-coupled data/ files, a fourth independent path to them.
    "tests/client/data/bus/use-orb-socket.test.ts",
    // #1243, packages/ui half: the SAME class as the client escapees above, on the OTHER package.
    // web-weave-*.test.ts bare-import "@orb/ui/web-weave" for pure geometry/physics (buildWeb,
    // WEAVE_TIMELINE, the Weave* types) - a .test.ts, not .tsx, so no packages/ui/tsconfig.json
    // reach-back claims it, and the barrel also carries the DOM-coupled web-weave.tsx component.
    // bar-list/option.test.ts deep-imports charts/bar-list/option.ts, which imports
    // charts/chart/{label-metrics,use-measured-width}.ts (DOM measurement). attach-media.test.ts
    // deep-imports the client feature file that imports "@orb/ui/file-dropzone" (a component barrel).
    "tests/ui/art/web-weave/web-weave-geometry.test.ts",
    "tests/ui/art/web-weave/web-weave-glint.test.ts",
    "tests/ui/art/web-weave/web-weave-physics.test.ts",
    "tests/ui/art/web-weave/web-weave-prey.test.ts",
    "tests/ui/art/web-weave/web-weave-render.test.ts",
    "tests/ui/art/web-weave/web-weave-spider.test.ts",
    "tests/ui/charts/bar-list/option.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/attach-media.test.ts",
    // #1243: two more reachers of data/bus/index.ts, via the DEEPER "@orb/client/data/bus" subpath
    // (not the top-level "@orb/client/data" barrel) - which still resolves to the impure index.ts
